id: pm-h85e
title: "GH-471: pm context includes an installed package/extension health summary"
description: "Dogfood GH-471: pm context shows item counts but nothing about extension/package health, forcing separate doctor/health invocations to understand project state. Duplicate check: searched context extension health summary — pm-ishm (GH-445) covers context tag noise only, no overlap."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[5]: agent-experience,"area:cli",context,extensions,gh-issue
created_at: "2026-07-06T21:09:04.826Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T19:41:44.037Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-03T19:40:19.423Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-03T19:40:19.423Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: pm context output includes a brief installed-packages line with health status (ok/degraded per package); stays token-lean and can be suppressed via a flag or --fields; covered by specs
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: medium
resolution: "PR #884 added bounded static extension_health projection to context output, healthy/degraded summaries, markdown and structured rendering, and a correctly normalized --no-extension-health CLI/SDK/MCP opt-out."
expected_result: "Context packets expose compact installed-extension health when packages exist, omit zero-value noise, preserve token budgets, and allow callers to suppress the projection."
actual_result: "Before this change, agents could not see extension degradation in normal context and had to run separate diagnostic commands, increasing context cost and delaying recovery."
